<!-- Content template version authority. The exact published version of the content template packages
     (Stride.Templates.Samples, .Games.Starters, .AssetPacks) this engine uses. Independent of the engine version and
     never composed with its prerelease suffix: the Game Studio bridge and the stride CLI resolve this version (or this
     checkout's -devN pack of it), and Stride.GameStudio depends on it. Don't edit it by hand: release-samples.yml sets
     it after publishing a samples release, so it always names content that is on the feed. Its major.minor follows the
     engine line and its patch part is a content counter (4.4.0, 4.4.1, ...), not an engine prerelease label; a
     prerelease (4.4.1-beta1) only marks content not ready yet, which a stable engine refuses to name. Keep the
     _StrideCommittedSamplesVersion line shape: the release workflows read and write it.

     Kept out of SharedAssemblyInfo.cs so a samples release rebuilds only Stride.Assets, not every assembly:
     Stride.Assets embeds this file as a resource (outside its reference assembly, so its dependents don't rebuild
     either) and the bridge reads the value from it. Imported by Stride.Templates.Common.targets (the pack side) and
     build/Stride.Samples.build (the samples release side).

     StrideSamplesVersion is the version a content pack gets (before the -devN worktree suffix). It defaults to the
     committed value; a -p:StrideSamplesVersion= global property wins (release-samples.yml packs the new number before
     it is committed). _StrideCommittedSamplesVersion always carries the committed value. -->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <_StrideCommittedSamplesVersion>4.4.1</_StrideCommittedSamplesVersion>
    <StrideSamplesVersion Condition="'$(StrideSamplesVersion)' == ''">$(_StrideCommittedSamplesVersion)</StrideSamplesVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
